SUMMARY:Progress and Inner Development
DESCRIPTION:Rosicrucians AMORC\, Santa Rosa\, CA\nRosicrucian Open Meeting
 . The public is welcome to attend.\n\n**Progress and Inner Development**\n
 \nWritten by: Robert E. Daniels\, F.R.C.\, for the *Rosicrucian Beacon\,* 
 June 2009\n\nIn this article\, the author describes how the Rosicrucian sy
 stem of study has three phases\, the study of our physical nature followed
  by the intellectual comprehension of Rosicrucian philosophy. Finally\, Fr
 ater Daniels details how the purpose of the third emotional phase is to de
 velop our awareness of the inner\, hidden parts of our being\, the so-call
 ed “psychic self\,” where we become more sensitive to our universe. Th
 is is also the most difficult phase for students on the mystical path beca
 use we have no yardstick to measure our progress and after some time and s
 tudy we come to the realization that the process is not a short one but ul
 timately one that provides great joy and deeper compassion for others.\n\n
 Presented by Dan Villalva\, F.R.C.\, Secretary for the Santa Rosa Pronaos.
 \nAll are invited to attend this lecture and discussion.\n\nAbout the Sant
 a Rosa Pronaos\nWe hold a monthly public presentation on mystical or metap
 hysical topics as a public service. The topics and speakers vary and no pr
 evious knowledge or experience is required. Just bring an open mind and he
 art.\n\nThe Santa Rosa Pronaos doesn't charge for admission. As always\, o
 ur events are free\, and donations are gratefully accepted to help defray 
 our costs.\n\nThe Santa Rosa Pronaos is a 501c3 educational non-profit\, a
 n affiliated body of the Rosicrucian English Grand Lodge for the Americas 
 and the Caribbean.
